    "description": "<h2 data-local-id=\"6f72577bc4a0\">Outcome and context</h2><p data-local-id=\"7149f531d307\">The associated-partner and associated-operator counts on the Account header are derived by concatenating partner record Ids into a 255-character text field and counting the semicolons. Eighteen-character Ids plus a delimiter fill that field at about thirteen entries, after which the value truncates mid-Id and the count silently under-reports. The rollup has no criteria either, so a partner whose deals all closed years ago still counts as associated.</p><p data-local-id=\"a2dc32d1101b\">Neither problem is visible yet at 28 deals and four partners. Both become visible as the org fills up, and neither is fixable in the current shape — a distinct count is not something DLRS does. Once relationship rows exist, both numbers are just a count of rows.</p><h2 data-local-id=\"09459aa89408\">Current state</h2><ul data-local-id=\"d8a98e9f2ccb\"><li data-local-id=\"8203f43debab\"><p data-local-id=\"4e0ed056e7e9\"><code>Deals_Operator_Associated_Partners</code> — DLRS Concatenate Distinct of <code>Deal__c.Partner__c</code> into <code>Account.Associated_Partners_List__c</code> (Text 255), delimiter <code>;</code>, Realtime, no relationship criteria. Mirror rule <code>Deals_Partner_Associated_Operators</code> into <code>Associated_Operators_List__c</code>.</p></li><li data-local-id=\"6c13d794141c\"><p data-local-id=\"ff9166548fc9\"><code>Account.Associated_Partners__c</code> and <code>Associated_Operators__c</code> are <strong>formula</strong> fields counting semicolons + 1, so they cannot be the target of a rollup.</p></li></ul><h2 data-local-id=\"c6dc6dd9939d\">Proposed solution</h2><ol data-local-id=\"c37f7793eca4\"><li data-local-id=\"a81fc73d05fd\"><p data-local-id=\"6359e434e05f\">Two DLRS <strong>Count</strong> rules on the relationship object into Account — one keyed on Operator, one on Partner — with criteria <code>Status__c = &#039;Active&#039;</code>. The Operator-side rule also carries <code>Is_Direct__c = false</code>, so the shared Direct record is not counted as one of an operator&#039;s partners.</p></li><li data-local-id=\"63cd24c464b2\"><p data-local-id=\"345a32924f20\">Replace the formula count fields. A formula field cannot be a rollup target, so each has to be deleted and recreated as Number. To keep the same API names — and avoid touching the header components and any report or list view referencing them — <strong>erase the deleted field from the deleted-fields list before recreating</strong>; the name is not available until it is erased. Recreating under a new name is the fallback and costs a downstream sweep.</p></li><li data-local-id=\"9dbca666cba8\"><p data-local-id=\"c2c2453d6933\">Deactivate and remove the two Concatenate Distinct rules and the two list text fields once the new counts are confirmed correct.</p></li></ol><h2 data-local-id=\"1554f4cc53c0\">Acceptance criteria</h2><ol data-local-id=\"fe622ab1adec\"><li data-local-id=\"a8e45bc2dbc9\"><p data-local-id=\"4a33379a7890\">An Operator with twenty active partner relationships shows twenty.</p></li><li data-local-id=\"6d9eb1c51309\"><p data-local-id=\"6faef04376ef\">An Operator whose relationships are all Inactive shows zero.</p></li><li data-local-id=\"4ed7fb0fd5e7\"><p data-local-id=\"4ff6483796d7\">An Operator with a direct arrangement and two partners shows two, not three.</p></li><li data-local-id=\"6260f7df078c\"><p data-local-id=\"45a1f55e3623\">Deactivating a relationship reduces the Operator&#039;s count with no edit to the Account.</p></li><li data-local-id=\"b28d3408c3c4\"><p data-local-id=\"05ef2c527705\">The Account header and every report or list view that referenced the old count still resolves after the change.</p></li></ol><h2 data-local-id=\"815ae8d2cf7c\">Out of scope</h2><p data-local-id=\"cfdb8b309f02\">Whether the Direct partner Account should display an operator count at all — a display decision for Kobi, not a build change.</p><h2 data-local-id=\"428fdf437705\">Dependencies</h2><p data-local-id=\"569be3aceb3c\">Depends on <em>Operator–Partner Relationship records created and deactivated from Deals</em>.</p><p data-local-id=\"3eb2adcb347e\">Supersedes the associated-partner and associated-operator header rollups as originally built; link the earlier header-rollup tickets to this one.</p>",
